The '''T-15''' was used by the [[Galactic Empire]] until it was rendered obsolete.

==History==
During the [[Mimban Campaign]], a [[swamp trooper]] reported to another that the T-15s were down, meaning they would have to walk.<ref name="Solo: A Star Wars Story">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

The T-15s were rumored to be marked obsolete by the time of the [[Battle of Scarif]], as discussed by two [[stormtrooper]]s right before being knocked out by [[Chirrut Îmwe]]. They implied when discussing this that they were looking forward to them being designated as such.<ref name="Rogue One: A Star Wars Story" />

==Behind the scenes==
The T-15 mentions in ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'' and ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'' were added by voice actor [[Sam Witwer]] as a reference to a conversation in {{Film|IV}} between two stormtroopers who are discussing the [[BT-16]] while [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] disables the [[tractor beam]]. Witwer also added similar lines in the [[sequel trilogy]], which mention the [[T-17]] and [[T-18]]. A similar reference to the [[T-16 skyhopper|T-16]] was added in "[[Part III]]" of the series ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]''. The mention depended on the era.<ref name="Sam Witwer">{{YouTube|video=Z8UdXvynS50|text=Sam Witwer - Matt Lanter - Star Wars Celebration 2022 - DAY 4 Panel|channel=UCX2BSSVDZbk5PrppNQREfTA|name=Super Steve|date=29-05-2022}}</ref>

